    {
      "old_claim": "Prior C1: p5 charges only PT-phase cycles; A's DDT/PDT walk, queue/HOL time are uncharged, so p5 understates A's true interference.",
      "corrected_claim": "Invalid. p5 charges each cycle ctl_did==DID_A in REQ_TRANS or AWAIT_RESP. In rv_iommu_trans_ctl_wrap, REQ_TRANS issues the translation request and AWAIT_RESP waits for trans_resp_valid_i, so the entire inner translator response (DDT/PDT/PTW) is inside the charged interval. COMPLETE is the only non-IDLE state excluded; IDLE is not busy. E2E is not a clean uncharged-occupancy measure because it also counts IDLE stale DID and all states.",
      "evidence": "cva6/corev_apu/fpga/src/ariane_peripherals_xilinx.sv:1000-1001,1022-1023; cva6/corev_apu/riscv-iommu/rtl/transaction_controller/rv_iommu_trans_ctl_wrap.sv:90-96,195-196,667-701,728-740; cva6/corev_apu/fpga/src/dma_research_policy.sv:290-293,328."
    },
    {
