      "corrected_claim": "Invalid. ctl_state_i is e3_ctl.state from rv_iommu_trans_ctl_wrap's trans_ctl_state_t (IDLE=0, REQ_TRANS=1, AWAIT_RESP=2, MRIF=3, COMPLETE=4); observer constants match this producer exactly. tl_wrap's enum is the inner translator and is not the consumer of ctl_state_i.",
      "evidence": "ariane_peripherals_xilinx.sv:1000,1022; rv_iommu_trans_ctl_wrap.sv:90-96,195; dma_research_observer.sv:76-80."
    },
    {
      "old_claim": "Prior C1: E2E can be compared with E32 to quantify uncharged A translator occupancy.",
      "corrected_claim": "Invalid as stated. ev_aown = ctl_did_i==DID_A with no state filter. e3_o.current_did is trans_req_data_q.did, and trans_req_data_q is only reloaded when IDLE accepts a new AW/AR; therefore IDLE can hold the stale previous A DID. E2E includes IDLE stale-DID cycles and all states, not just busy translator occupancy. COMPLETE-owned busy cycles are separately observable via cost_comp_q[1]/cur_a_comp; IDLE is not busy.",
      "evidence": "dma_research_policy.sv:58,199,294,451; rv_iommu_trans_ctl_wrap.sv:196,625-626,642-643,728-740; dma_research_observer.sv:432-433,974-1001,1517-1535; out/method-results-review-20261004/RESULTS.md:61-62."
